# Color Token Rule — BazaarPrinting CRM

**Never hardcode hex colors or rgba values in components.** Always use CSS variables defined in `app/globals.css`.

## Available Tokens

### Core UI
```
var(--color-bg)               Page background
var(--color-surface)          Card / modal / input background
var(--color-topbar)           Sidebar background
var(--color-border)           All borders and dividers
var(--color-text-primary)     Main body text
var(--color-text-muted)       Labels, placeholders, secondary text
```

### Accent & Buttons
```
var(--color-accent)           Primary accent (gold / orange)
var(--color-accent-dark)      Hover state of accent
var(--color-btn-primary-bg)   Primary button background
var(--color-btn-primary-text) Primary button text
var(--color-btn-verify-bg)    Verify / navy button background
var(--color-btn-verify-text)  Verify button text
```

### Semantic — Danger (red)
```
var(--color-danger)           Text / icon
var(--color-danger-bg)        Background
var(--color-danger-border)    Border
var(--color-danger-text-deep) Deep warning text (#7F1D1D light)
```

### Semantic — Success (green)
```
var(--color-success)          Text / icon
var(--color-success-bg)       Background
var(--color-success-border)   Border
```

### Semantic — Warning (amber)
```
var(--color-warning)          Text / icon
var(--color-warning-bg)       Background
var(--color-warning-border)   Border
var(--color-warning-text-deep) Deep amber text (#854D0E light)
```

### Semantic — Info (blue)
```
var(--color-info-bg)          Background (dedup banner, Known Customer, cold heat)
var(--color-info-text)        Text / icon
var(--color-info-border)      Border
var(--color-info-text-deep)   Deep blue text (#1E3A5F light)
```

### Semantic — Neutral (grey pill)
```
var(--color-neutral-bg)       Background (Pending, Not Defined)
var(--color-neutral-text)     Text
var(--color-neutral-border)   Border
```

### Tables & Badges
```
var(--color-row-alt)          Alternating row background
var(--color-row-hover)        Row hover background
var(--color-badge-bg)         Badge background
var(--color-badge-text)       Badge text
```

### Tabs
```
var(--color-tab-active)       Active tab text
var(--color-tab-underline)    Active tab underline
var(--color-tab-inactive)     Inactive tab text
```

## Reusable Components

Use these instead of inline urgency/status styles:
- `<StatusPill status={...} />` — for all lead/sales statuses
- `<UrgencyPill urgency={...} />` — for High / Medium / Low / Not Defined

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hardcoded hex
<div style={{ background: "#FEF2F2", color: "#DC2626", border: "1px solid #FECACA" }}>

// ✅ GOOD — token-based
<div style={{ background: "var(--color-danger-bg)", color: "var(--color-danger)", border: "1px solid var(--color-danger-border)" }}>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — inline urgency ternary
<span style={{ background: urgency === "High" ? "#FEF2F2" : "#FFFBEB", color: "#DC2626" }}>
  {urgency}
</span>

// ✅ GOOD — reusable component
<UrgencyPill urgency={lead.urgency} />
```

## Adding New Tokens

If a color is needed that isn't in the list above, **add it to `app/globals.css`** in both `:root` (light) and `.dark` sections before using it. Never use a raw hex in a component.
